task:
BUILD A READ-ONLY GOVERNED "HOST STORAGE DETAIL" OPERATOR ACTION. Base on current origin/main (record the SHA; it must include #832 at 24d0c4d9). New branch, no target_branch.

WHY: the v3-disk-inventory receipt of run 39018450185 (2026-10-17) shows /var/lib holds ~64.4 GB that is NOT the production PostgreSQL volume (edfinder-v3-phase4c-full-20260827_r5-pgdata, 1,346 GB). The owner wants to know what it is (Docker images, build cache, old Docker volumes from the August rehearsals, backups, ...) before deciding on cleanup. Nothing may be changed.

WHAT:
1. New script scripts/operator/actions/v3-host-storage-detail.sh, modelled on v3-disk-inventory.sh's safety posture (host identity check against deploy/v3-production/target-authority.json exactly as other read-only actions do; python3 -I -B standard library only; hard wall clock <= 600 s; no DB access; no writes anywhere except stdout). It reports ONE JSON receipt with:
   - `docker system df` totals (images, containers, local volumes, build cache: count, size, reclaimable) parsed from `docker system df --format '{{json .}}'`;
   - every Docker volume: name, labels, mountpoint, size in bytes (use `docker system df -v --format '{{json .}}'` Volumes section, or du of the volume mountpoint), whether any container (running or stopped) references it, and that container's name and state. The production pgdata volume must be reported by size from docker's own figure only, NEVER scanned with du;
   - every Docker image: repository:tag, id, size, created, whether any container uses it;
   - stopped containers: name, image, created, status;
   - `du -x -B1 --max-depth=2` of /var/lib, EXCLUDING /var/lib/docker/volumes/edfinder-v3-phase4c-full-20260827_r5-pgdata (pass --exclude for that exact path), sorted by size, top 40 entries;
   - presence and size of /var/lib/pgbackrest and /var/lib/ed-finder if they exist (du -sx -B1, same pgdata exclusion);
   - root filesystem df before/after; read_only=true; db_writes_performed=false; filesystem_writes_performed=false; status/failures fields like the other receipts.
2. Add operation `v3-host-storage-detail` to .github/workflows/chatgpt-ed-new-ops.yml (closed choice list + the operation allowlist case statement), wired like v3-disk-inventory (same ssh/elevation pattern, receipt to a runner.temp file, uploaded as artifact `v3-host-storage-detail-receipt`).
3. IMPORTANT, the owner and reviewer cannot download artifacts or read logs: after the action, the workflow must ALSO emit a compact human-readable summary as GitHub annotations using `::notice title=Host storage detail::<text>` lines (escape % as %25, CR as %0D, LF as %0A; keep each annotation under 4000 characters; at most 8 annotations). Summary content: docker system df totals; volumes sorted by size with in-use flag and container; images with size and in-use flag; /var/lib top entries. Generate the summary from the receipt with a small python3 -I standard-library snippet in the workflow step.
4. Tests: extend the existing ops-workflow contract tests so the new operation is in the closed list and allowlist, is read-only (no rm/prune/docker volume rm/docker rmi/docker system prune anywhere in the script), excludes the pgdata path from du, and the summary step escapes annotation text correctly (execute the summary snippet on a sample receipt in a test). Keep the authority gate passing: `python scripts/operator/v3_production_deploy.py --operation authority-gate` must report failures []. Update any operator docs/runbook listing of ops operations (search for v3-disk-inventory in docs/operations and mirror it).
Run ruff and the relevant pytest modules. Do not dispatch any workflow.
